### Summary of Changes
This PR implements a new custom matcher for Jest to be used when generating widget changes that need to be asserted.

This is quite useful when testing the outcome of running systems in a unit test.

The matcher is called `toContainChanges` and expects a widget id and a set of changes (i.e. a `Partial<SpecWidget>`).
It'll only be available when doing `expect` over a type that can be mapped to a `WidgetChange[]`, that is a single `WidgetChange`, an array `WidgetChange[]` or an `ActionList` instance.
For all other cases, the method should not even be suggested for use by intellisense.

Example:
```ts
describe('My Test Suite', () => {
  it('should have some prop in the changes', () => {
    const mySticky = defaultsApi.sticky();
    const initialStore = WidgetStore.fromWidgets([mySticky]);
    const currentStore = initialStore.apply(mySticky.id, { x: 100 });
    const widgetIds = [mySticky.id];

    const changes = runMySystem(initialStore, currentStore, widgetIds);
    
    expect(changes).toContainChanges(mySticky.id, { someProp: someValue });
  });
});
```

### Summary of Changes and Resources for the Reviewer

Push logs to datadog when a participant cannot `add` or `remove` a vote to help to track why votes are not syncing across all participants.

It includes `user, voting session, and widget` information.

No real `userId`'s are used. They all get replaced with a shortened uuid like `u12345678`

percivir/datadog logging docs: https://mural.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/RD/pages/2861334549/Percibir+-+Observability+Library

