The `workspaces` provided by WorkspacesStore never has counts and shouldn't be typed as WorkspaceWithCountsWithMembers.

The api query to fetch them passes `includeCounts=false` and the store's setWorkspaces() is typed as `WorkspaceWithMembers`.
```
export const fetchWorkspaces = (): Promise<WorkspaceWithMembers[]> => {
  return authenticatedGet(`/api/v0/workspaces?includeCounts=false`);
};
```

This pr formalizes `workspaces` to be typed correctly as `WorkspaceWithMembers`


### test-env 
https://workspacesstore-workspace-type.mural.engineering/

This is purely a CI change.

It adds a check that the versions of node declared in different places (package.json, dockerfiles, etc) are consistent and fails if they aren't.

It will print something like this:

```
> ../private-actions/node-consistency/get_node_versions.py
Dockerfiles have versions {'18.20.7'}
package.json files have versions {'18.20.7'}
package-lock.json files have versions {'18.20.7'}
Found .nvmrc file with version 18.20.7
```

